@startuml "MGL870 - Packages Rust"
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #606060
skinparam FontColor #404040
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 100
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
left to right direction

title "MGL870 — Organisation des packages Rust"

package "mgl870-benchmark-ipc" {
  [main.rs] as Main
  [models.rs\nTick] as Models

  package "rest" #E6F7FF {
    [Router REST\nAxum] as Rest
  }
  package "graphql" #E6F7FF {
    [Schema et mutations\nasync-graphql] as Graphql
  }
  package "jsonrpc" #E6F7FF {
    [Handler RPC\njsonrpsee + serde_json] as JsonRpc
  }
  package "grpc" #E6F7FF {
    [Service RPC\ntonic + prost] as Grpc
    artifact "proto/tick.proto" as Proto
  }
}

Main --> Rest : merge router
Main --> Graphql : merge router
Main --> JsonRpc : merge router
Main --> Grpc : tokio::spawn\nport 50051
Rest --> Models : désérialise Tick
Graphql --> Models : TickInput
JsonRpc --> Models : désérialise JSON
Grpc --> Proto : contrat généré
Grpc --> Models : TickMessage / TickList

note bottom of Main
HTTP/1.1 : port 8080
HTTP/2 : port 50051
end note

legend right
Le même binaire Rust expose les trois routeurs HTTP
et démarre le service gRPC. Chaque package conserve
la logique propre à son protocole, tandis que le modèle
Tick et le contrat proto définissent les données comparées.
end legend
@enduml
